From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:06:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: preserve desktop memory and display contracts

Port the fixed DRM pool and VRAM descriptors from Droid-VM
8daec4ee170115cb861db437017e56054de6eb5e, and detailed-timing
clock fitting from ac467c61410cb1790246ba8d36e65d5db9a1ae46.
Keep Linux's full DisplayID timing when the legacy EDID timing
needs reduced blanking or a lower refresh rate.

Accept the existing gpu-0 VNC binding and retain its normalized
pointer coordinates from 6455258e8d7eeb9050db3bc76dc14ed644b688a8.
Linux VNC continues to use its existing pixel coordinates.

BUG=None
TEST=ARM64 complete Windows GPU, macOS and Linux argument matrices
TEST=Six GPU descriptor/EDID tests and 12 display/input tests

Purpose: Preserve desktop memory and display contracts.
Origin: Droid-VM/crosvm commits cited above.
Upstream-Status: Downstream GunyahVM carry; not submitted to crosvm upstream.
